<div class="container my-5">

    <h1 class="text-center">Creating a Solution</h1>

    <p>
        Solutions are responses to clearly defined issues.<br />
        They propose ways to address, improve, or resolve a problem.
    </p>

    <p>Before submitting a solution, consider how it connects to the existing knowledge graph:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Which issue does this solution address?</li>
        <li>Is it a direct solution, a partial step, or part of a broader approach?</li>
        <li>Could it be one of several competing or complementary solutions?</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Positioning your solution correctly ensures it can be evaluated, compared, and built upon effectively.</p>

    <p>Content submitted here should be a structured solution, not a general idea or discussion post. A strong solution is:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>Clearly tied to a specific issue</li>
        <li>Thoughtfully explained</li>
        <li>Practical, testable, or actionable</li>
    </ul>

    <p>All submissions go through a moderation process to ensure they meet quality standards. This helps maintain clarity, consistency, and usefulness across the platform.</p>
</div>